Rem Linear regression functions coded in OPL for use from Psion
Rem Series3 calculator application.
Rem Copyright 1998 Daniel James.
Rem This code is made freely available for non-commercial use.
Rem Calculator memories M2..M9 are used.
Rem M9 = sum(x*y)
Rem M8 = sum(y^2)
Rem M7 = sum(x^2)
Rem M6 = sum(y)
Rem M5 = sum(x)
Rem M4 = N (the number of points)
Rem M3 = the slope of the line
Rem M2 = the intercept of the line (the y coordinate of the point
Rem where the line crosses the x axis).

Rem PROC calclr: is the top-level function. This is not called from
Rem the calculator but if CALCLR.OPO is accidentally run as an application
REM this proc will display a message.

PROC calclr:
	print "Regression calculations for Psion S3"
	print "Run these functions from the calculator!"
	print "N.B. Calculator memories 2-9 are used"
	print "Copyright ";chr$(&B8);" 1998, Daniel James."
	get
ENDP

Rem PROC pt:(x,y) is called from the calculator to add a new data 
Rem point (x,y). The poc updates the running totals in memories M4..M9

PROC pt:(x,y)
	m9 = m9+x*y
	m8 = m8+y*y
	m7 = m7+x*x
	m6 = m6+y
	m5 = m5+x
	m4 = m4+1
	return m4
ENDP

Rem PROC delpt:(x,y) is called from the calculator to remove an incorrectly
Rem entered data point (x,y).

PROC delpt:(x,y)
	m9 = m9-x*y
	m8 = m8-y*y
	m7 = m7-x*x
	m6 = m6-y
	m5 = m5-x
	m4 = m4-1
	return m4
ENDP

Rem PROC mx: returns the mean of the x coordinate values.

PROC mx:
	return m5/m4
ENDP

Rem PROC my: returns the mean of the y coordinate values.

PROC my:
	return m6/m4
ENDP

Rem PROC Clear: clears the calculator memories M2..M9, deleting all
Rem data points.

PROC Clear:
	M9 = 0
	M8 = 0
	M7 = 0
	M6 = 0
	M5 = 0
	M4 = 0
	M3 = 0
	M2 = 0
ENDP

Rem PROC LineFit: computes the slope and intercept of the straight line
Rem representing the best fit to the coordinate set represented by the
Rem values in M4..M9. The return value is the correlation coefficient R.

PROC LineFit:
	M3 = (m9-m5*m6/m4)/(m7-m5*m5/m4)
	M2 = (m6-m3*m5)/m4
	return m3*sdevx:/sdevy:
ENDP

Rem PROC FitX:(y) returns the x coordinate of the point on the line at the
Rem specified y coordinate.

PROC FitX:(y)
	return (y-m2)/m3
ENDP

Rem PROC FitY:(x) returns the y coordinate of the point on the line at the
Rem specified x coordinate.

PROC FitY:(x)
	return m3*x+m2
ENDP

Rem PROC sdevx: returns the standard deviation of the x coordinate values
Rem The 'sample' standard deviation calculation (N-1 weight) is used

PROC sdevx:
	return sqr( (m7-m5*m5/m4)/(m4-1) )
ENDP

Rem PROC sdevy: returns the standard deviation of the y coordinate values

PROC sdevy:
	return sqr( (m8-m6*m6/m4)/(m4-1) )
ENDP

